        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Low back pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Daytime pain is about the same, a mild ache that increases with prolonged sitting at a desk. Over the past 3–4 weeks, more aware of pain at night when trying to get to sleep. Pain is localized to the low lumbar area, right greater than left, non-radicular; dull ache with an occasional sharp twinge on extension or twisting in bed."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Sleep"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Takes longer to get to sleep; wakes 1–2 times to change position, then returns to sleep."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
